    `Father, I bring to You today the specific chapter I am in — the details that do not yet make sense, the closed doors I did not choose, the promises that have been delayed long enough to feel like denials. And I receive the sovereignty that Psalm 139:16 describes — the sovereignty that saw this chapter before it began, that has been present in every verse of it, and that is working in the specific details with the same intentionality You worked in Joseph's pit and prison. My purpose will stand. Let me hold that today not as a theological position but as the practical, lived trust of a person who has decided that the God who sees the end from the beginning can be trusted in the middle of the chapter that has not yet reached its end. You establish my steps. Even these ones.`
